            "text": "An efficient implementation that avoids high memory usage and timeout by computing pairwise distances in blocks using matrix multiplication in double precision (`float64`):\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    # Load vectors as float64 for high numerical precision and stability\n    X = np.load('vectors_secondary.npy').astype(np.float64)\n    n = X.shape[0]\n    \n    # Precompute squared norms: ||x_i||^2\n    sq = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', X, X)\n    \n    total = 0.0\n    batch_size = 1000\n    \n    for i in range(0, n, batch_size):\n        X_batch = X[i:i + batch_size]\n        b_len = len(X_batch)\n        sq_batch = sq[i:i + b_len]\n        \n        # ||u - v||^2 = ||u||^2 + ||v||^2 - 2 * <u, v>\n        dist_sq = X_batch @ X.T\n        dist_sq *= -2.0\n        dist_sq += sq_batch[:, None]\n        dist_sq += sq[None, :]\n        \n        # Explicitly zero the diagonal\n        for k in range(b_len):\n            dist_sq[k, i + k] = 0.0\n            \n        np.maximum(dist_sq, 0.0, out=dist_sq)\n        np.sqrt(dist_sq, out=dist_sq)\n        total += float(dist_sq.sum())\n        \n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
